Subject: [PATCH] dwrite: stop reading when a refreshed text source ends

Refreshing the final code unit can return a failed HRESULT, a null text
pointer or an empty chunk. text_source_get_u32_char() currently dereferences
that result even though text_source_read_more() can mark the context ended.

Stop iteration before dereferencing the refreshed chunk. This prevents the
DirectWrite exception observed during rekordbox 7.2.19 browser initialization
on Wine 11.18: text_source_get_u32_char+0x44 read through a null pointer,
Wine swallowed the window callback exception, and the library pane remained
black while the rest of the window still responded.

upstream/probes/dwrite-eof-test.c exercises normal text, end-of-text on a
refresh, and a failed refresh. The latter two crash the unpatched DLL and
return the supported one-character prefix with this change.

---
--- a/dlls/dwrite/analyzer.c
+++ b/dlls/dwrite/analyzer.c
@@ -436,8 +436,16 @@
     const WCHAR *text;
     UINT32 available;

-    /* Make sure to have full pair of surrogates */
+    /* Make sure to have full pair of surrogates. The source may return
+     * an error or end-of-text when refreshing the final code unit. */
     text_source_read_more(context);
+    if (context->end || !context->text || context->cursor >= context->chunk_length)
+    {
+        WARN("RBW-DWRITE: text source ended while refreshing a chunk.\n");
+        context->end = TRUE;
+        context->ch = 0;
+        return;
+    }

     available = context->chunk_length - context->cursor;
     text = context->text + context->cursor;
